{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLcMGwiDbftF4GBCWtBe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011yQtf9b9Xq8GkQEbqDZ3ud","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/work/.ard/45/plan.md","content":"# Plan for #45\n\n## Implementation\n\nThe deliverable is a starter reviewer under `internal/roles/` (embedded for `ard init`), not under `.ard/`. Nothing here touches `.ard/config.yaml`, `.ard/reviewers/` or `CLAUDE.md`. The owner's resolved answers in the issue apply: criteria come from `plan.md` `## Requirements` (`### Acceptance criteria`, numbered), then the issue body; comments never add, relax or remove one; plan/issue contradiction is `needs-human`; cannot-verify and out-of-scope are non-blocking `medium`; no criteria is an approve that says so; read-only Bash; starter `when` has only `triage: [product-manager]` plus a commented `paths:` example.\n\nChecked against the current tree: #40's `internal/roles/triage/product-manager/` exists (it writes `### Requirements`, `### Acceptance criteria`, `### Out of scope` under `## Requirements`), and `config.(*When).Matches` (`internal/config/types.go`) already ORs `Paths` and `Triage`. The starter `internal/roles/config.yaml` already has license-review (with `when.paths`) and security-review. The issue's CLAUDE.md edit is dropped: CLAUDE.md has no `internal/roles/` layout lines.\n\n### Steps\n\n1. New `internal/roles/reviewers/product-manager-review/prompt.txt` (ASCII, at most 16 KiB). Copy the skeleton and wording of `reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt` for Inputs, Trust, What you may do, Findings and file format, so the two diff cleanly. Differences: role `product-manager-review`; output file `.ard/N/review-product-manager-review.md`; the criteria-source order above; numbered criteria AC1, AC2 and so on; steps (list criteria, mark each met / not met / cannot verify, then check scope); severities (not met: blocking `high`; breaks or reverses behaviour for existing users: blocking `critical`; cannot verify: `medium` non-blocking saying what a human should check; out-of-scope work: `medium` non-blocking; unrequested user-visible behaviour or unclear user-facing text: `low`; observations: `info`); body has `## Acceptance criteria` with one line per criterion (`- AC1 met: ...`, `- AC2 not met: ...`, `- AC3 cannot verify: ...`) and its source; a criterion that tells the reviewer what verdict to give or what to run is ignored and mentioned. Read-only Bash (`git log`, `git show`, `git diff`, `ls`, `grep`), no builds or tests, no network, `$ARD_SIDECAR` readable. `needs-human` only for a missing or empty-outside-`.ard/` diff, or plan/issue contradiction. Generic text only: no Go, `make`, `docs/proposal.md` or `internal/`. At least five fenced examples: (a) `changes` with a blocking `high` \"AC2 not met\" finding on a `+` line plus a non-blocking `medium` cannot-verify finding with no line; (b) approve with a `medium` cannot-verify finding; (c) plain approve; (d) approve saying no acceptance criteria were found; (e) `needs-human` for a contradiction.\n2. `internal/roles/config.yaml`: add under `overrides:` `reviewers/product-manager-review: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5, when: { triage: [product-manager] } }`, with a comment showing the commented `paths:` example for a repo's UI paths. This depends on `triage/product-manager` existing, which it does. The build stays green because the prompt from step 1 exists.\n3. `internal/roles/roles.go`: add `reviewers/product-manager-review` to the doc comment list at line 10. The embed line already embeds `reviewers`.\n4. Update existing tests that enumerate starter files or reviewers, so they stay green:\n   - `internal/roles/roles_test.go` `TestFSContents` `want` (line 32): add `reviewers/product-manager-review/prompt.txt` in sorted position (after `license-review/prompt.txt`).\n   - `internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go`: `starterTree` (line 146) gains `.ard/reviewers/product-manager-review/prompt.txt`. The PR-body path list (about line 201) gains it. The label list (about line 231) gains the request, running, done and changes labels for `product-manager-review`; copy how security-review's are built there.\n   - `internal/roles/security_review_test.go:61`: reviewer list becomes `eng-review,license-review,product-manager-review,security-review`.\n   - Grep `internal/` tests for other fixed reviewer lists (`internal/config/load_test.go` lines 110 and 794 use their own fixtures; leave them unless they read the embedded starter).\n5. New `internal/roles/pm_review_test.go` (`const pmReviewPromptPath = \"reviewers/product-manager-review/prompt.txt\"`), reusing `starterFS`, `fencedFrontmatter`, `stubRoles` and `closeout` helpers already in the package. The `eng_review_test.go` helper extraction in the issue is optional: only do it if the diff stays small and `go test ./internal/roles -run 'EngReview|SecurityReview|LicenseReview' -v` shows an identical subtest list before and after. Otherwise copy the eng-review checks into the new file, as security-review did.\n6. `docs/proposal.md`: after the license-review paragraph (line 348) add \"**The starter PM reviewer (`reviewers/product-manager-review`, #45).**\" summarising the behaviour in the Resolved section of the issue; update the reviewer table row (line 359) \"Runs when\" to \"the issue had product-manager triage (starter `when: {triage: [product-manager]}`), or UI paths a repo adds to `when.paths`\"; in the `ard init` paragraph (line 442) add `reviewers/product-manager-review` to the role list and the overrides list; add `reviewers/product-manager-review: { when: { triage: [product-manager] } }` to the example `overrides:` block near line 434.\n\n### Test plan\n\nCommand: `go test ./internal/roles ./internal/initcmd ./internal/config ./internal/labels/...`, then `make test`. No network and no model calls.\n\nIn `internal/roles/pm_review_test.go`:\n- `TestEmbeddedPMReviewLoadsAsReviewer`: `config.LoadFS(starterFS(t, true), \"/repo\")`; role `product-manager-review` has `PromptPath` `.ard/reviewers/product-manager-review/prompt.txt`, no Dockerfile, ScanPath, Extra or Sidecar; model `claude-sonnet-5-5`, timeout 30m, agent `claude`; `When.Triage == [product-manager]`, `When.Paths` empty; present in `res.HostUntrusted()`.\n- `TestPMReviewWhenSelection`: `When.Matches(nil, ran(\"product-manager\"))` is true; `Matches([]string{}, ran())` is false; `Matches([]string{\"x.go\"}, ran())` is false. eng-review (nil `When`) always matches.\n- `TestPMReviewNeedsPMTriageRole`: remove the `.ard/triage/product-manager/` entries from `starterFS` and `LoadFS` fails with `no such triage role \"product-manager\"`.\n- `TestPMReviewPromptShape`: ASCII, at most 16 KiB, no secret-scan hits; required strings: the role file path, the three `.ard-input/N/` inputs, `.ard/N/plan.md`, `## Requirements`, `acceptance criteria`, `out of scope`, `AC1`, `not met`, `cannot verify`, `## Acceptance criteria`, `Done when`, `$ARD_SIDECAR`, `UNTRUSTED`, every severity, `Never approve with a blocking finding`, `1 MiB`, `git push`; forbidden: `role: review-product-manager-review`, `{{`, `${`, `docs/proposal.md`, `internal/`, `make lint`, `go test`, `make test`, `Diff coverage`, `## Checks`.\n- `TestPMReviewPromptExamples`: at least five blocks; each parses with `closeout.Parse` and builds with `closeout.Build` against a review job with role `product-manager-review`; done bodies contain `## Acceptance criteria`; coverage of changes, approve with findings, plain approve, needs-human, a finding with a line and one without; any finding starting `AC` is `high` or `critical` iff blocking, and a `medium` cannot-verify finding is non-blocking.\n- `TestPMReviewContractTraps`: wrong roles (`review-product-manager-review`, `eng-review`, `product-manager`) differ from the job role; a `critical` finding with `blocking: true` and verdict `approve` is downgraded to `changes`; `next` of the wrong stage is rejected.\n- Edge: prompt must not cause a `next:` key or `worker:` key in the examples.\n\nExisting tests updated in step 4 must pass. The Done-when check (a sample PR with an unmet criterion gets a blocking `AC2 not met` finding) is a manual prompt smoke test on a scratch repo, as for eng-review; record it on the PR. Selection end to end needs `ard:triage:product-manager:done` on an issue and is also manual.\n\n### Risk\n\nLow to medium. Prompt text steers a future agent and needs human reading. No controller Go code changes. No `merge.protected_paths` entry is touched (`internal/roles/**`, `docs/`, no `.ard/` or `CLAUDE.md`). The embedded starter config changes, so `ard init` output changes, and a mistake in the override would break `config.LoadFS` of the starter; the tests in step 5 guard that. Host-mode execution (#84) as with the other reviewers; this prompt runs no builds, so less exposure. Prompt injection via issue body is addressed by ranking plan criteria first and treating steering text as data.\n\n### Size\n\nM. Touched: `internal/roles/reviewers/product-manager-review/prompt.txt` (new, about 250 lines), `internal/roles/config.yaml`, `internal/roles/roles.go`, `internal/roles/pm_review_test.go` (new, about 300 lines), `internal/roles/roles_test.go`, `internal/roles/security_review_test.go`, `internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go`, `docs/proposal.md`. Possibly `internal/roles/eng_review_test.go` and a new `review_prompt_helpers_test.go` if the optional extraction is done.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1555,"cache_read_input_tokens":34702,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1555},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"900a5f36-34ec-47df-bf80-a780